CORE
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Constant folding of these divisions uses BigInt division. The scale factor that
normalises the divisor used to be computed as base / (1 + leading digit) in a
32-bit type, where the addition wrapped around to zero for a leading digit of
0xffffffff. CBMC then crashed with SIGFPE on x86, and folded the divisions to
wrong values on AArch64.
